          "why_it_matters": "The hook is what the quartet asks four strings to carry at once: improvisation, beat, counterpoint and several different American rhythmic lineages. RhythmNation moves through Threadgill, Jlin, Roumain, Diabaté, Mazz Swift and others while letting Janet Jackson's rhythmic vocabulary sit inside the same chamber-music frame. With the album freshly released in August, the DC date is a useful chance to hear how that recorded architecture breathes and changes onstage rather than simply a strong quartet playing a mixed-composer program.",
